<speak>
<s>This is your briefing for <say-as interpret-as="date" format="dmy">25052026</say-as>.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="95%">
<s>Riot police have seized Turkey's main opposition headquarters in Ankara under tear gas and rubber bullets, after a court voided the party leader's election and reinstated his defeated predecessor.</s> <s>Özgür Özel has appealed to the Supreme Court on whether judges can rewrite the outcome of an internal party ballot at all.</s> <s>What's at stake is whether Turkey's last institutional opposition retains the right to choose its own leadership.</s>
</prosody>
<p>
<s>In politics.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>India's Supreme Court has taken direct cognizance of the death of Twisha Sharma at her matrimonial home, with Chief Justice Surya Kant set to examine a delayed first information report, a disputed autopsy, and alleged interference in the probe.</s> <s>Madhya Pradesh has asked the Central Bureau of Investigation to take over.</s> <s>The bench is being asked to interrogate how police, postmortems, and paperwork systematically fail dowry-violence victims across the country.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Pope Leo the Fourteenth has issued an encyclical titled Magnifica Humanitas, binding the world's one point four billion Catholics to a formal teaching on artificial intelligence.</s> <s>An encyclical isn't commentary — it sets binding Church doctrine, and this one targets AI's toll on labour, human dignity, and the Global South.</s> <s>Dario Amodei of Anthropic, who's publicly opposed lethal autonomous weapons, attended the Vatican rollout.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Riot police in Dakhla, and Ryanair flights at thirty euros, are the visible edge of Morocco's strategy to convert tourism and budget capital into de facto sovereignty over occupied Western Sahara.</s> <s>The United Nations still classes the territory as non-self-governing, and the Sahrawi people have never voted on their future.</s> <s>Budget carriers and European holidaymakers are now the quiet underwriters of a settlement project the UN refuses to recognise.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Jamaat-i-Islami's Hafiz Naeemur Rehman has demanded Islamabad reopen the Chaman crossing into Afghanistan and legalise petroleum trade with Iran, framing border closures as economic asphyxiation of Baloch and Pashtun traders.</s> <s>It's the first time a mainstream religious-political party has owned a position usually voiced only by separatists.</s> <s>Rehman warned of a nationwide strike after Eid al-Adha if the crossings stay shut.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>West Bengal has ordered the construction of statewide holding centres for Rohingya and Bangladeshi nationals, under a detect, delete, and deport policy.</s> <s>Bangladesh accepts almost no deportees, which turns India's centres into indefinite warehouses for stateless people.</s> <s>About five hundred and fifty kilometres of the two-thousand-kilometre West Bengal border remain unfenced.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Eight Arab and Muslim-majority states — including Pakistan, Somalia, and Egypt — have condemned Somaliland's plan to open an embassy in Jerusalem.</s> <s>Israel recognised Somaliland in December and remains its sole state backer; no other government extends recognition.</s> <s>The condemnation is rare because it names a single breakaway capital rather than the wider conflict.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Benin's Romuald Wadagni has been sworn in with ninety-four percent of the vote, after the main opposition parties were barred from competing.</s> <s>Wadagni served as Patrice Talon's finance minister and ran as the sole approved candidate.</s> <s>The opposition holds no legal route back — the same threshold that cleared the field now governs the country.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>On the economy.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Singapore's first-quarter GDP grew one percent on AI-driven electronics demand, even as the trade ministry named Iran-war energy prices as the primary downside risk to its full-year forecast.</s> <s>It's the split that matters — chip and data-centre exports are absorbing a global slowdown that's draining other small economies.</s> <s>Whether the electronics buffer holds through a longer Gulf conflict is the question now hanging over Southeast Asia.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Petrol in Delhi has crossed one hundred and two rupees a litre — the highest level since two thousand and twenty-two — after the fourth hike in eleven days.</s> <s>India's oil retailers had held pump prices frozen for four years, and the Strait of Hormuz blockade has now added seven and a half rupees per litre in cumulative increases since mid-May.</s> <s>Congress has begun calling Prime Minister Modi the inflation man, and his government's offered no price relief.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Armenia has opened rail trade with Turkey via Georgia for the first time, using the Akhalkalaki–Kars corridor that's sat barred since it was built in two thousand and seventeen.</s> <s>The opening flows from the post-two thousand and twenty Azerbaijan peace process.</s> <s>Prime Minister Pashinyan said direct rail links to Azerbaijan itself will follow, in sha'Allah.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Mohammed bin Salman's signature megaprojects — NEOM, The Line, and Qiddiya — are in quiet retreat, as Saudi Arabia's one trillion dollar sovereign wealth fund proves unable to sustain all three at the scale he decreed.</s> <s>Oil revenue, US deal pressure, and the Iran war have drained the pipeline that funded Vision twenty-thirty.</s> <s>What survives, and at whose expense, is now Mohammed bin Salman's choice alone.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>In Darfur, a sheep that fetches four hundred and fifty thousand Sudanese pounds at source sells for above two million in central Sudan, as war-blocked roads trap livestock supply in the south.</s> <s>Eid al-Adha demand is peaking, and traders are pressing both sides to reopen the corridors.</s> <s>Sudan now also runs two central banks — the Rapid Support Forces' Mustaqbal Bank serves territory the official bank has abandoned, and analysts warn the monetary split risks permanent partition.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In science.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Ebola has killed three Red Cross volunteers in eastern Democratic Republic of the Congo, in an outbreak caused by the Bundibugyo strain — for which no approved vaccine exists.</s> <s>The virus has crossed into Uganda, which has confirmed five cases, and Africa's Centres for Disease Control has placed ten countries on watch.</s> <s>Frontline responders are dying because the strain sits outside the cold-chain product the world spent a decade building.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>The Antarctic Treaty's annual meeting has again failed to protect the emperor penguin, even as sea-ice loss collapses its breeding habitat.</s> <s>Middle powers like Australia, Chile, and Norway hold legal tools within the treaty system to mandate protection short of consensus, but none has yet invoked them.</s> <s>Which state moves first will tell us what climate governance is actually for.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>A Nature Communications study has found that an automatic carbon floor inside the EU emissions trading system would have blocked the two thousand and twenty-two gas-to-coal switch without raising consumer bills.</s> <s>The mechanism is empirical — a reserve price on carbon allowances changes producer incentives faster than discretionary intervention.</s> <s>Whether Brussels adopts it before the next gas shock arrives remains unresolved.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>In Somaliland, seventy-four percent of consumers buy vegetables from informal markets where no pesticide withdrawal periods are observed and no residue testing exists.</s> <s>Eighty-six percent of farmers surveyed lacked any food safety information, and the region has no residue standard at all.</s> <s>It's a quiet, structural exposure that touches every meal eaten in the Horn.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In technology.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Huawei has told an academic conference it'll reach one point four nanometre transistor density by twenty thirty-one — under sanctions that locked it out of the lithography tools required to get there conventionally.</s> <s>Its Tau Scaling Law routes around US export controls through chip stacking and wiring-path folding, not smaller transistors.</s> <s>Kirin chips due in fall of next year will be the first mass-production test of LogicFolding.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>High Bandwidth Memory now accounts for sixty-three percent of the cost of a leading AI chip, up from fifty-two percent just two years ago, according to Epoch AI.</s> <s>That places South Korea's memory makers — SK Hynix and Samsung — and not TSMC or Nvidia, at the chokepoint of global AI capacity.</s> <s>Epoch concluded that memory export controls now carry more leverage over AI buildouts than restrictions on logic chips.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>In Solomon Islands villages, single Starlink dishes are being pooled across whole communities, because individual subscriptions cost more than monthly household income.</s> <s>It's an informal mesh that emerged from the gap between Low Earth orbit pricing and Pacific wages.</s> <s>Whether Pacific regulators formalise community sharing or move to restrict it will decide what connectivity actually means in the Global South.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Anthropic's Glasswing project has reported finding over ten thousand critical software vulnerabilities in a single month, with Cloudflare alone uncovering two thousand bugs at a lower false-positive rate than human reviewers.</s> <s>Patching, not detection, is now the bottleneck, and full disclosure awaits the fixes.</s> <s>AI is producing flaws faster than vendors can close them.</s>
</p>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="90%">
<s>That's your briefing.</s>
</prosody>
</speak>